  "title":                "Audio Scene Management V1.0",
  "Header":               "CAE-ASM-V1.0",

  "Identifier":           {"ImplementerID": "/* String from IIDRA */", "ImplementationID": "/* String from Implementer */", "AIMName": "CAE-ASM-V1.0"},

  "APIProfile":           "Basic",
  "Execution":            "Continuous",
  "Description":          "Audio Scene Management: an audio chain - Audio Object Editing, then Audio Scene Editing - and a speech chain - Speech Object Editing, then Speech Scene Editing - whose Scenes Multimodal Scene Editing (OSD-MSE) composes into a Multimodal Scene; each AIM with its own User Command, each returning the User Command with its response (how each action was executed). Every edit is a new version in the Module's Shared Storage, from which Objects and Scenes are opened by their identifiers. Speech Object Editing has a Speech Object translated by Text and Speech Translation (MMC-TST); the translation replaces the original, under its identifier, so every Speech Scene holding it holds the translation, at its place. Capture, reading the User's stored Objects, and hearing the Objects and Scenes - Audio and Speech Object Delivery - are the User Agent's, through the Units of its Physical Layer. The User Agent submits the User Commands to the command Port it addresses by Data Type and Port Number, so that the Controller, and only the Controller, decides which of the editing AIMs it reaches. Audio Scene Management Interface (CAE-AMI) is the one AIM that touches the boundary of the Composite: the Ports of the Composite are its left-hand Ports, and it serves the Editing AIMs from its right-hand Ports as the boundary served them. It also takes the commands of an application interface - an Application JSON Instance (MMC-AJI), on the User AJI Input Port - and answers them in an Application JSON Instance, on the User AJI Output Port. A vocal interface (recognition of spoken requests, understanding them as User Commands, speaking the replies) is not part of this Module: it is an extension to be specified.",

